# Commit message template — enable with:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Format
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   <body: what changed and why, wrapped at 72 columns>
#
#   Agent: <agent-id>
#   Agent-Role: <role>
#   Module: <MODULE-ID>
#   Refs: #<issue-or-pr>
#   Validated-With: <exact command(s) and result>
#
# Types: feat fix refactor perf docs test build ci chore revert spec ux contract
# Scope: a MODULE-ID (e.g. AUTH-001) — or `repo` for repository-wide changes.
#
# Rules
#   * One coherent change per commit.
#   * Agent/Agent-Role/Module trailers are REQUIRED on branches under agent/*.
#   * Never claim validation you did not run.
#   * Subject in the imperative mood, no trailing period, <= 72 chars.
#
# Example
#   feat(AUTH-001): implement password reset flow
#
#   Adds a single-use, expiring reset token issued through the notification
#   port so no mail provider is hard-wired into the auth module.
#
#   Agent: impl-auth-001
#   Agent-Role: implementation
#   Module: AUTH-001
#   Refs: #42
#   Validated-With: python scripts/verify.py (exit 0), 14 tests passed
